#[
    -------------------------------------
    ------ SELF-HOSTED DRAGONSTONE ------
    -------------------------------------
    ------------ MAIN ENTRY -------------
    -------------------------------------
]#

#[

    This is the main entry point for the Dragonstone 
    Programming Language.

    This initializes the CLI and starts the execution 
    process. It will handle command-line arguments and 
    manage input/output streams. It will return an integer
    exit code upon completion.

    #! This file might not change after Self-Hosting is 
    #! complete. But, this is what is being used in the
    #! current version of Dragonstone to start the 
    #! bootstrapped version of Dragonstone.

    #! Although there is an easier way to do this, I made
    #! this route as it's more explicit and easier to 
    #! understand.
    
]#

use "../src/dragonstone/cli/sh_cli"

module Dragonstone
    extend self 

    define main: int
        return Dragonstone::CLI.run(
            args = nil, 
            out  = nil, 
            ex   = nil, 
            in   = nil
        )
    end
end

quit Dragonstone.main
